    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d291">

                <pb facs="0399" n="331" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v01/pg331"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72/2143½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Wilson to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-09-13">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">13 September, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I have read this
                    carefully.</p>
                <p>I think the course we orally outlined this morning is the best one:</p>
                <p>To let this particular vessel go upon a promise by the British Admiralty and a
                    bond by the owners of the vessel that the arms will in no case be used for
                    offense;</p>
                <pb facs="0400" n="332" xml:id="pg332"/>
                <p>And to prepare the general regulation you suggest., but not publish it or put it
                    into effect until we see what we are going to be able to work out of this <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Arabic</hi> business.</p>
                <p>Faithfully Yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W.W.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
